            "reply_markdown": "Sorry for the trouble signing in. Here are some steps that usually fix missing MFA prompts:\n\n1. Check your phone has a data or Wi-Fi connection — prompts can't arrive in airplane mode.\n2. Open the authenticator app directly. A pending request often shows there even if no notification appeared.\n3. Check notifications are allowed for the authenticator app in your phone settings, and that Do Not Disturb/focus mode isn't blocking them.\n4. Check your phone's date and time are set to automatic — a clock that's off by a few minutes can cause failures.\n5. Fully close the authenticator app, reopen it, and start a new sign-in attempt on your laptop.\n6. If the app offers a six-digit code, choose **Use a verification code instead** on the sign-in page and enter it.\n\nIf none of this works, please reply with which phone and authenticator app you use. If you've recently changed phones, let us know as that needs a separate process.",
